cff-version: 1.2.0
title: malayalam-factcheck-corpus
message: >-
  If this corpus or pipeline is useful in your work, a citation using
  the metadata below would be appreciated. Where it fits, a citation
  to the underlying fact-check publishers (mapped via the source_id
  field on each record) alongside this one is appreciated too, since
  the verdicts and evidence originate with their reporting.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Hrishikesh
    family-names: Bhaskaran
    email: hello@stultus.in
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9502-401X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/stultus/malayalam-factcheck-corpus"
url: "https://github.com/stultus/malayalam-factcheck-corpus"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19940702
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.19940702
    description: Concept DOI (resolves to the latest archived version on Zenodo)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.19940703
    description: Version DOI for v0.1.1
abstract: >-
  A reproducible batch pipeline that ingests Malayalam fact-check
  articles from IFCN-certified Indian portals and produces a
  versioned, deduplicated Parquet corpus of (claim, verdict, evidence)
  triples for training claim-verification and misinformation-detection
  models. Source-attribution and verdict provenance are preserved on
  every record.
keywords:
  - misinformation
  - fact-checking
  - claim-verification
  - malayalam
  - indian-languages
  - low-resource-nlp
  - dataset
license: MIT
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-05-01"
